<details><summary>Original description</summary>

```markdown
validate_pilot.py builds the requested arms from real traces into a dry-run prefix. It re-decodes every row independently: trained spans equal the GLM turns, there is no loss on padding or past a row's content, and held-out status matches the arm. It reports each build's wall time and peak memory. Dry-run prefixes carry a DRY_RUN_NOT_FOR_TRAINING marker and never get _SUCCESS.

verify_arms.py re-reads production prefixes. It checks:
- the markers, and every file and row hash against the manifest;
- row counts, steps and padding;
- per-family token totals;
- that no row comes from a held-out task;
- that every epoch holds plain's replay rows;
- that plain's epochs are the same rows in different orders;
- that RS-multi's epochs are within 1% of B on plain's task slots.

progress.py dry-builds plain, RS-multi and relay over every finished generation shard. progress_table.py renders that summary as a dated table with per-family projections and flags: B above the replay ceiling, relay below parity, an unknown drop reason, or a capability-token drop.

verify_arms.py passed on the pool v5 plain and RS-multi prefixes.

